  "details": "<p><em>The Barrington Atlas Directory</em> notes: villa, near Vesunna?</p>\r\n<p>Primuliacum is associated with Sulpicius Severus, an early Christian ascetic, who was a native of Aquitania. By the late fourth century, Sulpicius Severus had converted his villa at Primuliacum into a Christian retreat.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Now unlocated, Primuliacum was located in southwestern Gaul.",
